# 1640s horse (2026-10-18): Prince Rupert's cavaliers - straight at whatever is in front, and after
# the beaten wherever they run.
drill "Gallop"
era 1640s
about "Rupert's cavaliers: straight at whatever is in front at the gallop, sword in hand, and after the beaten wherever they run."
type Harquebusier
dials aggression 0.98 discipline 0.30 cohesion 0.50 cover 0.00 patience 0.20 nerve 0.70

sergeant:
  when enemy within 140                                  -> charge
  otherwise                                              -> advance fast

man:
  otherwise                                              -> charge
